# the wasm reader, bytes into the wasm model
#
# the header is checked, then the sections are walked in file order, each
# bounded by the size it declares. a section id the specification has not
# assigned, a section out of the order it fixes, a section running past the
# end of the file and a vector count larger than the bytes left in its
# section are refused, as each stops the reader from bounding the file or
# sizing a table. everything inside a bounded section that does not parse,
# a code the tables do not name, a type the reader does not decode or bytes
# left over after the last record, holds the section or the subsection raw as
# unsupported, with every table as it was before the decode began. a custom
# section no convention names is held raw as opaque.

